  "limitations": [
    "This approval is scoped to P12/G12. It proves exact continuation acceptance, scheduling, and one dequeue by the logical successor; it does not claim that the scheduled application command ran or that its success condition was fulfilled. P14 owns that application/MCP execution boundary.",
    "The standalone session-host executable is a bounded one-shot P12 surface and truthfully reports manager_ipc_available=false. P16 owns persistent Manager IPC and final process composition.",
    "The WinHTTP tests use a bounded local test provider. P15 owns LM Studio discovery, deployment, and external-provider qualification.",
    "Under OWNER-002 the Validator reviewed the one authoritative command and hashes without a duplicate rebuild. Release configuration, clean-environment reproduction, alternate machines, dedicated security hardening, installer qualification, UI automation, and bespoke visual polish are outside G12 and remain assigned to their later or deferred gates.",
    "Passing G12 is not a claim that the Windows application or owner-qualified internal alpha is complete."
  ],
